{
  "id": "R003Z",
  "version": "2.0",
  "title": "CT scan",
  "description": "A CT (computed tomography) scan creates detailed cross-sectional images of your body to diagnose conditions like cancer, infections, injuries, or organ disease. This outpatient procedure uses X-rays and computer processing to build precise pictures. Depending on what your doctor is evaluating, you may receive contrast dye (through IV, mouth, or enema) to highlight specific areas and improve image clarity. You'll lie still on a table that slides through the scanner for 5-10 minutes. The procedure is painless and you go home immediately after. The cost of this procedure may vary depending on the imaging protocol used. Options include without contrast, with contrast, with and without contrast, breast ct, and bone density study.",
